# Resizable panels (`react-resizable-panels` v4)

Applies when using [`ResizablePanelGroup`](../../frontend/components/ui/resizable.tsx) / [`ResizablePanel`](../../frontend/components/ui/resizable.tsx) in production UI (not Storybook-only demos).

## Size props (critical)

Numeric props are **pixels**; strings without units are **percent** (see library `PanelProps` in `node_modules/react-resizable-panels`).

| Intent | Correct | Wrong (common bug) |
|--------|---------|---------------------|
| Min ~35% of group | `minSize="35%"` | `minSize={35}` → 35 **px** |
| Min 260px document column | `minSize={260}` | `minSize={26}` → 26 **px** (crushed column) |
| Max 55% | `maxSize="55%"` | — |

Always document px vs `%` in code comments when both appear on one screen.

## SSR / hydration

The library sets **non-SSR-safe inline styles** on `Panel` (flex, min/max height). Do **not** render `ResizablePanelGroup` on the server.

**Pattern (reference):** [`store-sales-form-desktop-split.tsx`](../../frontend/app/[locale]/(admin)/admin/(backoffice)/sales/store/_shared/store-sales-form-desktop-split.tsx) loaded from the page via `next/dynamic(..., { ssr: false, loading: () => <Skeleton…> })`. Keep a small skeleton ([`store-sales-form-desktop-split-skeleton.tsx`](../../frontend/app/[locale]/(admin)/admin/(backoffice)/sales/store/_shared/store-sales-form-desktop-split-skeleton.tsx)) aligned with route `loading.tsx`.

Do not rely on `useMounted()` alone if the resizable tree was ever in SSR HTML — prefer `ssr: false` for the split module.

## Group and panel layout (page scroll)

Library defaults fight full-page scroll and card ring clipping:

| Layer | Library default | Warehouse override |
|-------|-----------------|-------------------|
| Group | `height: 100%`, `overflow: hidden` (not overridable) | `style={{ height: "auto" }}` on `ResizablePanelGroup` |
| Panel inner wrapper | `overflow: auto`, `maxHeight: 100%` | Panel `className`: `overflow-visible! max-h-none!` |
| Inner content | — | `min-w-0`, `overflow-x-hidden` on wrappers; `h-full min-h-0` when columns should stretch |

Use `className="… items-stretch"` on the group so both columns share row height.

**Sticky sidebar:** `position: sticky` on content **inside** the group does **not** work like member edit grid — the group’s `overflow: hidden` creates a containing block. Do not promise viewport sticky while using this library unless the sticky node lives **outside** the group (different layout).

## Persisted layout

- Group `id` + `defaultLayout` + `onLayoutChanged` → `localStorage` (v4; not `autoSaveId`).
- **Sanitize** saved percent shares on load/save (reject extreme ratios from old bugs or corrupt JSON).
- Reference constants: `store-sales-form-split` group id; panels `store-sales-browse` / `store-sales-document`; default 60/40.

## Column height parity (split forms)

When the right column is a tall card (header + flex body + footer):

- Browse column root: `md:h-full md:min-h-0`
- Growing card (e.g. product step): `md:flex-1 md:flex md:flex-col md:min-h-0`
- Document card: `md:h-full`
- Panel inner wrappers: `h-full min-h-0`

Mobile stacked layout (`md:hidden`) must not depend on `h-full` on the same nodes.

## Toolbar rows beside narrow columns

When a toolbar sits in a resizable column, **do not** `flex-wrap` inside the search input + submit button group. Match design [`order-store-form__search-group`](../../design/css/style.css): one flex row for input + button; category/filter are **sibling** flex items that wrap as whole groups (`flex-[0_1_10rem]` for category, not `flex-1` on the same row as search).

